File Index

/hudThemeStore.ts
Purpose: Manages the single HUD theme preference ('default' | 'slate-amber') stored in localStorage — consolidated from the former separate hudLayoutStore (classic/compact) + hudThemeStore (default/slate-amber) pair; layout and visual skin are now one selectable unit per theme, not two independent settings. 2026-09-20 (live theme switching): setHudThemeId now also DispatchEvents HUD_THEME_CHANGED_EVENT after the localStorage write, so MainContainer.tsx's ListenEvent subscription can apply a theme change live (same-tab — native `storage` events never fire same-tab) instead of requiring a reload.

/themeRegistry.ts
Purpose: THEME_REGISTRY maps each HudThemeId to a ThemeDefinition (lazy-loaded ShellComponent, optional NarrowShellComponent + narrowBreakpoint, loadStyles); resolveActiveTheme(themeId, viewportWidth) is the pure resolution function MainContainer calls every render — picks a theme's own narrow variant below its breakpoint if it has one (both 'default' and 'slate-amber' do now — CompactLayoutShellNarrow.tsx for the latter), else falls back to 'default's shell AND styles (a generic fallback for whichever future theme skips building a narrow variant, no longer exercised by either registered theme — see themeRegistry.test.ts for a test that still exercises it directly). Each theme's `loadStyles` just sets `data-hud-theme` on `document.documentElement` — the actual CSS (e.g. styles/hud/themes/slateAmber.theme.scss) is a plain side-effect import bundled into whichever of that theme's shells actually loads, gated behind that attribute; there is no runtime `<link>`-swapping (retired with hudThemeLoader.ts). `onActivate` (separate from `loadStyles` — plugin lifecycle, not visual) is the theme→plugin auto-enable hook; `slate-amber`'s calls `pluginHost.enable('world-time-and-identity')`. Wired from a `MainContainer.tsx` effect placed AFTER the plugin-registration effect specifically — `pluginHost.enable()` on an unregistered id silently no-ops, so ordering matters here and isn't just stylistic.

/hudWidgetRegistry.ts
Purpose: In-memory registry where plugins publish/clear content into named compact-HUD widget slots (ownership-checked clears, dispatches an update event); also owns ALL_HUD_SLOT_IDS, the runtime list of valid slot ids (relocated here from @shatteredarchive/types-client so a stale/missing dist/ there can't leave it undefined at runtime).
